# Project identity (canonical paths)

## Canonical repository

Always treat this path as the application repository root / checkout / working directory:

`/home/ysh/thealltour`

Never use these as repository root, checkout, `WorkingDirectory`, deployment source, or app cwd:

- `/home/ysh/theallcloud` <!-- canonical-path-documented-forbidden -->
- `~/theallcloud` <!-- canonical-path-documented-forbidden -->

Default generated commands, systemd units, and ops docs to `/home/ysh/thealltour` unless a subsystem documents a different path.

## Path vs legacy identifier

| Kind | Rule |
|------|------|
| Filesystem / repository path | Use `thealltour` (`/home/ysh/thealltour`) |
| Legacy logical identifier | May remain `theallcloud` — do **not** global-replace |

Keep unless explicitly instructed to change:

- `ORCHESTRATION_PROJECT_ID="theallcloud"`
- MCP server id `theallcloud-marketing`
- Other documented compatibility aliases (e.g. gateway `theallcloud/auto`)

## Other canonical paths (do not swap with app repo)

- Marketing asset root (Hermes-Pi): `/mnt/HDD2TB/marketing-assets`
- Mini-PC shortform workspace: `/home/ysh/.cache/thealltour-shortform/`
- Embedding repo: `/home/ysh/thealltour-ai-inference`

## Mandatory preflight

Before repository work, verify:

```bash
pwd
git rev-parse --show-toplevel
```

Expected root: `/home/ysh/thealltour`

If another root is detected, **stop and report** — do not silently adapt paths.

Executable guard: `npm run check:canonical-paths`
